  "question": {
    "text": "For a particle in uniform circular motion the acceleration $\\vec{a}$ at a point $P(R, \\theta)$ on the circle of radius $\\mathrm{R}$ is (here $\\theta$ is measured from the $x$-axis)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "D9FSX",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\cos \\theta \\hat{i}+\\frac{v^2}{R} \\sin \\theta \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lxR1d",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\sin \\theta \\hat{i}+\\frac{v^2}{R} \\cos \\theta \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IulZD",
      "text": "\n$-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\cos \\theta \\hat{i}-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\sin \\theta \\hat{j}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "LI1RT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{v^2}{R} \\hat{i}+\\frac{v^2}{R} \\hat{j}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For a particle in uniform circular motion,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}^2}{\\mathrm{R}} \\text { towards centre of circle } \\\\\n& \\therefore \\quad \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}^2}{\\mathrm{R}}(-\\cos \\theta \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}-\\sin \\theta \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}) \\\\\n& \\text { or } \\quad \\vec{a}=-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\cos \\theta \\hat{i}-\\frac{v^2}{R} \\sin \\theta \\hat{j} \\\\\n&\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/kP0H7gFebMfdqUaFix_vbN8v0l76pkJk50cDFNvcdPI.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
